fact WorkItem(id: "WI-943", description: some(value: "An OPERATION type parameter has TWO canonical unification vars, and every reader must know which one it is holding.\n\nMEASURED 2026-08-02 while fixing WI-942 (see rustland/anthill-core/src/kb/typing.rs, the `op_param_rigids` loop in `check_operation_bodies`). For `operation cmp[T](a: T, b: T) -> Int64 requires Ordered[T]`:\n  * `OperationInfo.type_params` holds `Var::Global(1325)` -- minted at load, and what `rigidify_op_type_params` binds when it skolemizes the body;\n  * the param SYMBOL `...cmp.T` aliases (SortAlias) to `Var::Global(1)` -- what a WRITTEN occurrence of `T` resolves through (`type_param_global_var`), hence what `sigma_class` sees inside the `requires Ordered[T]` clause.\nFor a SORT parameter the two COINCIDE (`sort_type_params_as_pairs` IS the alias table), which is why the split stayed invisible: every sort-param reader is right by accident of the two being one var.\n\nWHAT IT COST. WI-942: the σ bridge (`canonical_global_var`) was built from one identity and consulted with the other, so `op_requires_covers` could not see that an operation's own `requires Ordered[T]` covers its own `Ordered.compare(a, b)`. It refused the program at load, demanding a `requires` `on enclosing sort` that the author had already written on the OPERATION. WI-942 fixed it by recording BOTH identities against the same rigid -- correct, but it is a bridge over a split that should not exist.\n\nWHY THIS IS NOT MERELY COSMETIC: the two-identity split is exactly the shape of defect this repo keeps re-finding (one question, two answers, agreeing only where the names coincide). Any future reader of an op type param picks an identity and is silently right or silently wrong depending on which. `declared_type_param_vid` / `type_param_vid_in_sort` / `sigma_class` take the alias one; `rigidify_op_type_params` / `check_unconstrained_type_params` take the record one.\n\nSCOPE: decide whether the two can be made ONE var (make the illegal state unrepresentable), or -- if they genuinely must differ -- give the pairing ONE owner with a doc-commented invariant, so no reader has to know. NOT root-caused: I did not read where the SortAlias for an op type param is asserted versus where OperationInfo.type_params is minted; that is the first question.\n\nACCEPTANCE: driven, not just loaded -- a test that resolves an op type param through BOTH routes and asserts they agree, plus the WI-942 tests (renamed_op_type_params_are_covered_by_the_operations_own_requires in particular) still green with the WI-942 double-recording REMOVED if the identities are unified. cargo-test green.\n\nSOURCE: found by WI-942, which works around it."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-08-03T10:55:34Z"))
